 "notes": "Official length 186.2 km (letour.fr / cyclingstage: Côte de Loucrup 50.9, sprint Pouzac 59.1, Côte de Mauvezin 77.3, Col d'Aspin 118.1, Col du Tourmalet 147.8). The Hautes-Pyrénées itinéraire horaire (185.6 km) lists every point exactly 0.6 km lower, so itinerary km + 0.6 is used throughout. km 0 (départ réel) is placed at the D37/D802 junction in Mazères-Lezons (43.2784, -0.3550), 0.6 km before the itinerary's own départ-réel point on the D802 rocade ('à 7,7 km du lieu de rassemblement'); the neutralised section from Pau via Jurançon and Gelos is not included. Route: D802 rocade (Franqueville tunnel), D938 expressway past Idron, Meillon, Assat, Bordes, Boeil-Bezing and Mirepeix (all 'près'), through Coarraze, D937 from Igon (près) via Lestelle-Bétharram, Saint-Pé-de-Bigorre and Peyrouse; D13 into Lourdes (Route/Rue de Pau, rond-point Michel Crauste, Av. Gén. Baron Maransin, Place du Marcadal, Rue de Bagnères, Bd du Lapacca); D937 via Lézignan, Arcizac-ez-Angles, Escoubès-Pouts and the Côte de Loucrup (cat. 4) to Montgaillard (Route de Lourdes Prolongée); D935 via Trébons and Pouzac (intermediate sprint) into Bagnères-de-Bigorre (Av. du Général Leclerc, Place Lafayette, Rue Maréchal Foch against the one-way as given in the town's road-closure notice, Rue du Général de Gaulle); D938 Route de Toulouse past Haut de la Côte, La Coume and Cieutat (the D938 passes south of the village), l'Escaladieu, Côte de Mauvezin (cat. 3), Capvern; D929A from Avezac-Gare, D929 via Hèches, Rebouc and Sarrancolin to Arreau; D918 over the Col d'Aspin (cat. 1), Payolle, Sainte-Marie-de-Campan, Col du Tourmalet (HC), Barèges, Luz-Saint-Sauveur; D921 via Gèdre to Gavarnie; the finish is 0.7 km up the D128 route des Espécières. Placement: itinerary points sit on the routed road at their official km, interpolated between firmly located anchors (km 0, junctions, summits, finish). In several villages the itinerary km falls 0.6-1.7 km before the centre (the timing schedule appears to use the village entry). There the official point is named '… – itinerary point', and a separate town point at the centre carries a km derived from routed distance (medium confidence). Points named 'via …' only keep a shortest-path router on the race road (hairpins, parallel streets); their km is derived. Routed length through all waypoints on Overture 2026-10-21.0 roads is about 187.4 km (+0.6 %). Uncertain: between Bagnères and l'Escaladieu the itinerary splits (Bagnères→Cieutat 7.2 km, Cieutat→l'Escaladieu 7.0 km) fit the map poorly. The D938 south of Cieutat was assumed; the loop through the village (Marque Dessus / Era Coustéta) would add about 0.8 km. No sprint-line coordinate is published, so the Pouzac sprint is placed by km.",
